WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.735
New developments in the special counsel's

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.303
criminal investigation

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.204
into Donald Trump's

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.539
handling of classified documents.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.575
Josh Dawsey of The Washington Post

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.642
helped break the story.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.710
He's joining us now.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.911
Josh, tell us what you and

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.614
your colleagues are now learning.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.148
Right, Wolf.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.049
So what we're learning

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.517
is that one day before

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.986
federal authorities came tomorrow

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:23.289
I go last June to pick up

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.291
classified documents

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.427
and returned to a first subpoena.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.063
That video camera footage shows

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.098
two Trump employees,

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.333
two employees of the former

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.801
president, Mar a Lago

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:35.935
Porter convoys

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.438
moving boxes back into his storage room.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.939
As you remember,

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:40.573
when the fourth

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.909
when the feds arrived at Mar a Lago.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.144
Trump's team

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.678
said, come with us to the storage room.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:46.713
That's what the documents are.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.014
You can do a search.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:49.616
They would not let them in the boxes

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.884
but what we've reported

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.353
is that the boxes were previously moved

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.122
after forcibly not arrived.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.058
And then the night before,

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.359
federal officials

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.894
came to Mar a Lago,

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.630
they were put back into the storage room.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.532
We're also reporting that

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.300
federal investigators

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.935
probing the classified document

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.770
the handling of former President Trump

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.806
have multiple witnesses who told them

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.274
he displayed

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.241
classified information

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.109
to visitors

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.945
and left it out and showed it to others.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.282
And we're also reporting that before

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.284
this time where they do

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.352
not give the documents back,

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.287
they went through

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.021
what was called

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.656
an apparent dress rehearsal,

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.458
according to a federal judge,

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.293
when the National Archives

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.295
asked for the documents back before.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.696
So are of the same playbook on

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:37.997
how not to get the documents back.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.599
Was what they did

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.601
with the National Archives as well.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.302
So, Josh,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.237
how could this inform possible

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.538
criminal charges?

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.174
Well, Wolf, what we're

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:48.808
reporting is

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.009
that the investigation

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.212
is in its final stages,

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:52.779
at least right

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.481
now, that the grand jury meeting

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.883
to understand what happened

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.218
and whether to just to see

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.953
getting indictments

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.955
has not met and several weeks.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:04.124
Most key witnesses have been interviewed.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.392
And what we see now

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.861
is that a lot of the investigation

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.462
is not about

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.196
the former president

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.265
taking the documents originally,

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.234
but is about efforts to get them back,

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.168
how those efforts

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.803
were potentially obstructed,

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.871
why the former president

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.873
did not want to give the documents back,

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.942
and whether or not at Mar a Lago,

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.844
the documents were mishandled.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.746
If you remember correctly,

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:27.480
the former president,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.149
whose team had previously said,

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.484
you know,
these were just boxes in a storage room.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:32.752
But what we're learning

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.255
now is that it was a lot more than that.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.523
And there was a comprehensive effort

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.290
behind the scenes

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.259
to keep a lot of these documents.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.693
And some of these documents

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.695
were not just in a storage room.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.664
They were being showed to visitors

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.698
at the Florida resort

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.033
at home of the former president.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.501
You know,
that's a very, very serious

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.202
development indeed.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.870
Josh, I want you to stay with us.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.971
I also want to bring in

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.640
our legal analysts to discuss.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.241
And Laura Coates, I'll start with you.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.809
How do prosecutors view

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.077
the timing of all of this

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.946
moving boxes of documents

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.815
the day before the FBI came to Mar a Lago

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.817
to retrieve these top secret

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.186
classified documents

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.822
with an eye towards prosecution.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.391
One of the most complicated things

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:12.959
you have to do as a prosecutor

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:13.893
is try to get into

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.428
the mind of the person

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.229
who might be the target

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.531
of your investigation. To prove intent.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.066
You have to really do so

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.701
with circumstantial evidence,

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.836
with contextual clues and beyond.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.306
But if you actually have some evidence

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.340
direct evidence

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.075
that the person was aware

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.476
that you wanted something

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.178
that you were entitled to have

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.880
and went through specific steps

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.015
to actually prevent you from having that.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.418
That's definitely channel obstruction.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.052
And so

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.019
it gets to the meat

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.521
of the matter of intent.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.690
The idea of doing a practice run

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:47.393
also buttresses the prosecutorial eye

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.361
in this case.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.028
And remember,

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.263
the attorney for Donald

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:50.763
Trump

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.498
had already had his attorney

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.267
client privilege pierced

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.269
because they thought it was

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.071
entitled to do so under the crime fraud

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.006
exception that he may have been directed

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.040
to somehow lie

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.642
to the people who wanted the document.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.810
Do they had the right to have

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.712
and also to direct others to do the same.

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:06.246
And so

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.914
this is really forming

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.983
a substantive case of intent

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.185
you otherwise would not be able to get

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:14.654
if you had to hypothesize or opine

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.123
what possibly this person was thinking.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.358
And Norm Eisen,

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:20.426
on this so-called dress rehearsal

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.094
where Trump

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:23.229
allegedly reviewed the contents

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.864
of some of these boxes.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.165
How much does that speak

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.835
to intent Intent, which is very important

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:29.769
in your view?

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:32.939
Well, Wolf,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:33.740
in addition to

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.174
the words of Donald Trump

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:37.343
himself, to illuminate his intent,

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.812
you look to actions

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:42.782
and to have a dress rehearsal

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.284
that prosecutors may

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.385
well characterize

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:46.252
as a dress

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.454
rehearsal, for obstruction

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.523
is just such damning evidence.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.026
And to be able to present

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.494
that to the jury,

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.262
it brings that case to life.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.563
Donald Trump was already

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.565
in a tremendous amount of trouble

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.601
before these latest revelations,

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.702
but they have deepened

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:05.438
that peril even more.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.372
And Paula Reid

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.740
what will the special counsel

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.675
and the Justice Department,

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:09.542
for that matter,

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:10.743
need to weigh here,

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.645
considering whether to bring

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.681
obstruction charges, for example?

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.549
There are a lot of questions here, right?

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.617
We know the day before the

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.452
this Justice Department visit

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.421
that one of his attorneys, Evan Corcoran,

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:23.022
you folks have already referenced here,

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.358
he was searching for classified documents

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.426
and they need to know, okay,

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:27.493
why were these moving?

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.127
Were these moving?

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.029
Because they needed to get out of the way

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.030
during the search.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.198
Was this a normal part

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.900
of looking for classified documents

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.368
or was this intentional?

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:36.636
If it was intentional?

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:37.337
Well,

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:39.472
who directed these boxes to be moved?

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.607
Why were they directed to be moved?

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:42.875
Where did they go?

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.110
A lot of questions again

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.411
about intent here.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.347
Why these boxes were moving in and out

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:49.148
if it wasn't just a normal course

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:49.982
of trying to search

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.451
through this storage room.

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:52.919
But even if prosecutors

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:53.853
come to the decision

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.355
that they do want to pursue

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:57.256
potential charges of obstruction,

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.124
what we've seen with

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.692
this Justice Department

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:00.760
is the attorney general.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.196
Again,
he doesn't make the first decision here,

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:04.130
Jack Smith will.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.064
But this attorney general

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:06.265
has not shown an interest

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:07.367
in pursuing cases

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.301
that are just about

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.602
obstruction of justice

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.504
without another underlying crime.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:12.772
So even if they find evidence

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:13.740
of obstruction,

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.707
the next question is

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:15.842
whether they find evidence

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:18.177
of any other potential underlying crimes,

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.278
because that's the way

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:21.013
so far we've seen in other high

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.448
profile investigations

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:23.649
that this Justice Department

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:26.185
has preferred to advance Interesting.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:26.886
And Josh,

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.020
I want you and our viewers

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.088
to listen and watch

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:29.655
what former

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.824
President Trump told our Kaitlan Collins

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.826
at CNN's recent town hall

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:35.595
When it comes

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:36.496
to your documents,

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:37.463
did you ever show those

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.365
classified documents to anyone?

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.032
Not really.

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:41.300
I would have the right to.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.936
By the way, they were demystified after.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:46.272
Not that I can think of.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:47.573
I'm sorry.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.841
Let me get your thoughts on that.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.376
That doesn't seem to line up.

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:50.977
Or does it

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:51.811
line up with what

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:54.180
your reporting seems to line

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:56.082
I didn't hear. I know there did.

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:59.218
You know, that sounded not really

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:01.654
and not that I recall,

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:03.456
but I would have the right to do that.

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:05.691
I mean,
that was a very interesting answer.

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:06.993
And what federal prosecutors

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:08.661
have learned from other witnesses

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:09.962
is that he did show

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.063
classified documents

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:12.465
and that he did

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.534
keep some out in his office.

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:17.937
So his answer on there was noncommittal.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.605
And I think there might be a reason

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:20.339
for that.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:21.240
So, Laura,

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:21.974
what does that say

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.476
about where the special counsel

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:24.343
Jack Smith's

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:26.279
criminal investigation stands?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:28.514
Well, they were

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:29.682
likely salivating

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.217
through that answer, as we discussed

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.084
that very night,

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:34.153
the idea that somebody would be giving

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.455
a jigsaw piece

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:36.889
puzzle a puzzle piece

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:39.125
right to the hands of the special counsel

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:40.426
on potentially an area,

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.727
they were not clear about what

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:43.062
they are likely to be

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:44.363
crystal clear on

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:46.265
is the Presidential Records Act

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.401
and who the documents belong to

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:49.502
and what the requirement

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:51.270
is to declassify documents.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.005
It's not just the waiving of a wand.

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:54.140
As he went on to talk about

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:54.874
and the idea of

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:55.842
he can be classified

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:56.709
with a snap of a finger.

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.377
And of course, I'm paraphrasing,

00:07:58.377 --> 00:08:00.046
but it also is about the substance

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:00.813
of the information.

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:02.081
I remind the viewers,

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:04.016
we still do not sitting here

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:06.118
know the full breadth and scope

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.687
or the underlying content

00:08:07.687 --> 00:08:08.788
of all the documents.

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:09.188
We're talking

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:10.556
about thousands, though,

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:11.224
that contrast

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:13.226
with what they originally handed over,

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:14.427
what the attorney said, that

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:16.462
they had finished the handing over

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:17.830
and what ultimately they recovered

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.499
from a duly executed

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:21.501
search warrant of the Mar a Lago estate.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:22.101
And so

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:23.936
you've got some unanswered parts here,

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.605
but you have the connective tissue

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:26.672
once again

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:27.440
of somebody

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.775
directly stating what they did.

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:30.376
So, Norm,

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.111
what do you expect in the coming weeks

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:33.179
and months, for that matter?

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:37.483
Well, it does seem

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:42.021
by every external indication that the Mar

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:42.421
a Lago

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:45.391
documents case is coming to closure.

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:47.827
The evidence is powerful.

00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:49.929
It is not just the obstruction evidence.

